# The same fight as the tests, played many times. There is not a card in it: the player has two
# abilities on cooldowns, so this is what `cantrip sim` has to keep working for a turn-based
# roguelike rather than a deckbuilder.
#
# Nothing here rolls a die — the Ghast cycles its moves — so every run goes the same way, and the
# report says so rather than pretending that 200 runs measured more than one.
#
# It also reports that Screech never fires: the Ghast is wounded before its turn comes round, and
# the wounded phase re-telegraphs, so the move at the end of its pattern is never reached. That is
# the sort of thing this is for.
#
# Run:  dotnet run --project src/Cantrip.Cli -- sim samples/abilities

scenario "The Ghast, with Cleave and Brace"
  runs 200

  player hp 40
  grant Cleave, Brace

  battle Ghast

  expect no stalls
  expect no errors
